  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p style=&quot;margin-bottom:6.0pt; margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm; margin-top:6.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height:normal&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt&quot;&gt;1. The proposed development, by reason of its design, massing, roof profile and building form would fail to deliver high-quality design and would introduce unduly dominant, bulky and an unsympathetic building which would be out of keeping, and at odds with, the character and scale of the immediate properties and the surrounding street scene, to the detriment of the character of the area. As such the application is not in compliance with Policy 53 and Policy 8 of the Waltham Forest Local Plan (2024) or the London Plan, Supplementary Planning Guidance – Housing (2016), Living with beauty, promoting health, well-being and sustainable Growth, The report of the Building Better, Building Beautiful Commission (Jan 2020) and National Design Guide: Planning practice guidance for beautiful, enduring and successful places (Jan 2021), call upon ensuring high quality developments are forthcoming.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin-bottom:6.0pt; margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm; margin-top:6.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin-bottom:6.0pt; margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm; margin-top:6.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height:normal&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt&quot;&gt;2. The proposed rear balcony on top of of the ground-floor rear projection would compromise the amenity of the occupants at no.222 Sinclair Road, as well as no.315 and 317 Hall Road by creating harmful overlooking and a loss of privacy. As such the application is not in compliance with Policy 57 of the Waltham Forest Local Plan (2024).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin-bottom:6.0pt; margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm; margin-top:6.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin-bottom:6.0pt; margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm; margin-top:6.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height:normal&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt&quot;&gt;3. Notwithstanding the first reasons for refusal, the applicant has failed to enter into a S106 agreement and therefore is not in compliance with Policies 60, 61, 62, 81 and 94 of the adopted Waltham Forest Local Plan LP1 (2024), Policies T1, T2, T3 and T4 of the London Plan (2021) and Supplementary Planning Document – Planning Obligations (2017), specifically in relation to the following planning obligation requirements:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin-bottom:6.0pt; margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm; margin-top:6.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin-bottom:6.0pt; margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm; margin-top:6.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height:normal&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt&quot;&gt;(i) Financial contribution of £500 towards CLP monitoring.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin-bottom:6.0pt; margin-left:0cm; margin-right:0cm; margin-top:6.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;line-height:normal&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt&quot;&gt;(ii) Pre and post construction condition survey, and for the developer to pay for any subsequent remedial works resulting from damage from the site construction phase.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
